IMPORT prelude

-- Protection of Word "Anzac" Act 1920 (Cth) — THE NOUNS, THE RULES AND THE
-- TOP-LEVEL GOAL. Source: ../registers/source-bundle/C1920A00054.txt
-- (compilation of 28 February 2014). The person using the word asks: "If my
-- use of 'Anzac' breaches the Regulations, what is the most I can get?"

§ `Nouns`

-- s 22(2)-(3): the use made of "Anzac" or a word resembling it.
DECLARE `Use of the word` IS ONE OF
    `in connection with a trade, business, calling or profession`
    `in connection with an entertainment, lottery or art union`
    `as the name of a private residence, boat, vehicle, or charitable or other institution, or a building connected with it`
    `as the name of a street, road or park`
    `another use`

-- Which provision of the Protection of Word "Anzac" Regulations is breached.
DECLARE `Breach` IS ONE OF
    `subregulation 2(1)`
    `subregulation 3(1)`
    `another regulation`
    `no breach`

DECLARE `Anzac case` HAS
    `my use`                IS A `Use of the word`
    `the breach`            IS A `Breach`

DECLARE `Anzac penalty` IS ONE OF
    `imprisonment for up to 12 months`
    `the penalty the Regulations set, a fine of at most $1,000`
    `no penalty`

§ `Rules`

-- s 22(2): a breach of subregulation 2(1) by a use in connection with a trade
-- etc., an entertainment, lottery or art union, or as a name of the listed
-- kinds: imprisonment up to 12 months.
@ref s 22(2)
GIVEN c IS A `Anzac case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 22(2) applies to` c IF
        c's `the breach` EQUALS `subregulation 2(1)`
    AND NOT (c's `my use` EQUALS `as the name of a street, road or park`)
    AND NOT (c's `my use` EQUALS `another use`)

-- s 22(3): a breach of subregulation 3(1) by a use as the name of a street,
-- road or park: imprisonment up to 12 months.
@ref s 22(3)
GIVEN c IS A `Anzac case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 22(3) applies to` c IF
        c's `the breach` EQUALS `subregulation 3(1)`
    AND c's `my use` EQUALS `as the name of a street, road or park`

@ref s 22
@export default The most a person can get for using the word "Anzac" (or a word resembling it) in breach of the Protection of Word "Anzac" Regulations, under s 22 of the Protection of Word "Anzac" Act 1920 (Cth): imprisonment for up to 12 months for a breach of subregulation 2(1) by a use in trade, business, a calling or profession, an entertainment, lottery or art union, or as the name of a private residence, boat, vehicle, institution or building (s 22(2)), or of subregulation 3(1) by naming a street, road or park (s 22(3)); otherwise the penalty the Regulations set, at most a $1,000 fine (s 22(1)(g)). Whether there is a breach is an input. DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Anzac case`  @desc How I use the word, and which regulation it breaches
GIVETH A `Anzac penalty`
`the Anzac penalty for` c MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF c's `the breach` EQUALS `no breach` THEN `no penalty`
        IF `section 22(2) applies to` c OR `section 22(3) applies to` c THEN `imprisonment for up to 12 months`
        OTHERWISE `the penalty the Regulations set, a fine of at most $1,000`
